CONFIRMED FINDINGS (1):
- unicode-case-collision-wrong-table: two SQLite tables distinct only by a
  non-ASCII case pair (KÖLN vs köln) collide to one Trino identifier. Trino
  lowercases with Unicode rules; getTables matches with ASCII-only COLLATE
  NOCASE. Result: SHOW TABLES / information_schema list only ONE table (the
  other is unreachable), and SELECT * FROM "KÖLN" silently returns köln's rows.
  WRONG TABLE + silent metadata data-loss. Deterministic 3/3.

SEED VERDICTS:
- Case-insensitive table/column resolution: ASCII "T"/"t" and "A"/"a" collisions
  are a FALSE PREMISE (SQLite itself rejects them). The constructible, real bug
  is the Unicode variant above (FILED). Single mixed-case names resolve fine.
- Quoted names / spaces / dots / unicode: mixed-case resolves fine; Unicode
  case-collision is the filed bug.
- Hidden sqlite_* excluded correctly; user table named "sqlite" (6 chars)
  correctly included; views + quoted names resolve correctly. No bug.
- query() passthrough SAFETY: claim HOLDS in practice — bare INSERT/CREATE/
  writing-PRAGMA fail at metadata probe; "...;..." trailing statements rejected
  (syntax error); INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE...RETURNING pass the probe but fail at
  execution because the fetch wraps the query as FROM (<q>) o. No write ever
  landed (md5 + row counts unchanged). BUT the connection is actually READ-WRITE
  (getConnection override drops setReadOnly(true)); safety rests solely on
  subquery-wrapping. Documented as LATENT RISK in NOTES.md (not a confirmed
  wrong-rows/write bug).
- query() returns same rows as table scan; computed columns -> VARCHAR with
  correct values; comments inside query work. No bug.
- getColumns: cid ordering + NULLABLE from notnull consistent; no type
  mis-report found.

